{%- set first = variants.0 -%}
{%- set darks = variants | filter(attribute="variant.appearance", value="dark") -%}
{%- set lights = variants | filter(attribute="variant.appearance", value="light") -%}
# {{ theme.name }} bat Theme

[bat](https://github.com/sharkdp/bat) themes for {{ theme.name }}. {{ theme.description }}

## Installation

1. Create the themes directory:

   ```bash
   mkdir -p "$(bat --config-dir)/themes"
   ```

2. Copy the theme file(s) to the themes directory:

   ```bash
{% for v in variants %}   cp {{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}.tmTheme "$(bat --config-dir)/themes/"
{% endfor %}   ```

3. Rebuild the cache:

   ```bash
   bat cache --build
   ```

4. Verify the theme is available:

   ```bash
   bat --list-themes | grep -i {{ theme.id }}
   ```

## Usage

```bash
# Use once
bat --theme="{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}" <file>

# Set as default (add to shell config)
export BAT_THEME="{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}"
```
{% if darks | length > 0 and lights | length > 0 %}
You can also use `--theme-dark` and `--theme-light` for automatic switching:

```bash
export BAT_THEME_DARK="{{ theme.id }}-{{ darks.0.variant.id }}"
export BAT_THEME_LIGHT="{{ theme.id }}-{{ lights.0.variant.id }}"
```
{% endif %}
